    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Calculate the integral $\\int 4{e}^{6x}{({e}^{6x}+5)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's introduce the new variable $u={e}^{6x}+5.$ Differentiating gives \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6{e}^{6x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\text{d}u=4{e}^{6x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4{e}^{6x}{({e}^{6x}+5)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {({e}^{6x}+5)}^{3}\\cdot 4{e}^{6x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{3}\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\int {u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\frac{{u}^{4}}{4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{({e}^{6x}+5)}^{4}}{6}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
