    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{{6}^{z}}{\\sqrt{{6}^{z}-6}}\\,\\text{d}z.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's introduce the new variable $u={6}^{z}-6.$ Differentiating gives \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}z}={6}^{z}\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}\\,\\text{d}u={6}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{6}^{z}}{\\sqrt{{6}^{z}-6}}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{6}^{z}-6}}\\cdot {6}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{1/2}}{(\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{{6}^{z}-6}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
